cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below. Once the associated
  manuscript is accepted, cite the paper instead and add its DOI here.
title: Impact of Rock Anisotropy on Tensile Strength and Modes of Rupture
abstract: >-
  Orthotropic stress analysis and four-mechanism failure classification for
  Brazilian tensile tests on foliated rocks. The workflow solves the
  Lekhnitskii Airy-series stress field for a transversely isotropic disc,
  classifies failure pointwise into weak-plane tensile, weak-plane shear,
  matrix tensile and matrix shear, traces diagnostic crack trajectories, and
  partitions strain energy across those classes. It covers fourteen specimens,
  seven fabric orientations in each of an augen gneiss and a psammitic schist,
  and reproduces every table and figure of the associated manuscript from the
  raw measurements.
